# Noujoude — Prettier exclusion list.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (it is a safety control, not a style preference):
# `package.json` ships `"format": "prettier --write ."`. Prettier parses Markdown
# and JSON, and this repository's read-only source documents are Markdown. With no
# ignore file, a single well-intentioned `pnpm format` would rewrite the files under
# `reference/` — which Directive §3 places off limits ("Never modify, rename,
# overwrite, or delete original source files") and which `docs/REFERENCE_INTEGRITY.json`
# fingerprints, so the rewrite would also trip the preflight DRIFT check and invalidate
# every `line N` citation in `docs/` (ARCHITECTURE_DECISIONS §8: citations are addressed
# to these exact bytes).
#
# `pnpm format:check` (`prettier --check .`) is the gate that CI runs; it never writes.
# `pnpm format` is the developer's fixing command and is only safe because of this file.

# ─── Read-only inputs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Authoritative sources. Never reformatted, never rewritten, never renamed.
reference/
# Original asset library. Preserved byte-for-byte; 82/82 SHA-256 re-checked on every
# preflight run. `_manifest.json` inside it is evidence, not a file to beautify.
Noujoude.photo/

# ─── Unknown-provenance root file ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Present in the workspace before this build; preserved untouched by standing rule
# ("inspect the actual directory, preserve unknown files"). Not ours to reformat.
README_Noujoude_Master_Specification_EN111.md

# ─── Generated evidence artefacts ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Machine-written by scripts/. Byte stability matters more than formatting, and a
# reformat would make a regenerated artefact diff against its own previous run.
docs/CITATION_VERIFICATION.json
docs/REFERENCE_INTEGRITY.json
docs/DOCX_MD_ALIGNMENT.json
docs/asset-audit-summary.json
docs/ASSET_INVENTORY_AUDIT.csv
docs/CITATION_TRIAGE_2026-10-31.superseded.txt
# Verbatim command transcripts. Their value is that they are the bytes a run produced;
# any formatter touching them would make the evidence unquotable.
docs/A5_PRIVILEGE_EVIDENCE.txt

# ─── Tool output and installed trees ─────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
pnpm-lock.yaml
*.tsbuildinfo
